From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: do not report absent flow counters as zero

The NPU firmware rejects the per-flow statistics block with -22 and the
driver carries on without counters, which is the right call: counting is
optional and must not cost us the offload.  What is left over is the
reporting.  /sys/kernel/debug/ppe/entries still prints packets=0 bytes=0
for every bound entry, because the readout returns early and leaves the
caller's zero-initialised struct alone.

A bound entry carrying traffic and printing zero is worse than printing
nothing: it invites the conclusion that the flow is not being offloaded,
when the opposite is true.  Print the counters only when the driver owns
a working statistics path, and say so explicitly otherwise.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
@@ -162,11 +162,21 @@
 		*((__be32 *)h_source) = cpu_to_be32(l2->src_mac_hi);
 
 		seq_printf(m, " eth=%pM->%pM etype=%04x data=%08x"
-			      " vlan=%d,%d ib1=%08x ib2=%08x"
-			      " packets=%llu bytes=%llu\n",
+			      " vlan=%d,%d ib1=%08x ib2=%08x",
 			   h_source, h_dest, l2->etype, data,
-			   l2->vlan1, l2->vlan2, hwe->ib1, ib2,
-			   stats.packets, stats.bytes);
+			   l2->vlan1, l2->vlan2, hwe->ib1, ib2);
+
+		/* When the statistics block is not available the counters are
+		 * absent, not zero, and printing 0 there reads as "this flow
+		 * has forwarded nothing" - the opposite of the truth for a
+		 * bound entry that is carrying traffic.
+		 */
+		if (ppe->foe_stats_enabled)
+			seq_printf(m, " packets=%llu bytes=%llu",
+				   stats.packets, stats.bytes);
+		else
+			seq_puts(m, " packets=n/a bytes=n/a");
+		seq_puts(m, "\n");
 	}
 
 	return 0;
